      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I recall someone changed the voltage scaling mode after the original implementation. So, I believe this comment is now wrong.\n\nThings to note:\n\n* On reset VOS3+64MHz is the default scaling+clock. So, following this code path on clock_init is okay.\n* The original code enabled VOS3 with the HSI/64MHz. See line 181 of the original code.\n\n---\n\nI\u0027m not saying I agree with all of these setting or that they are completely correct. This implementation is simply a \"functional equivalent\". We will get to optimizing in a followup CL.\n\nThese types of comparisons are checked using https://crrev.com/c/2096017 .\nI ran the test again. In the following screenshot, you can see the test results from before this change. The right panel is after this change.\nhttps://pasteboard.co/IZSqHpA.png",
